Z||000005||Raydar||03-30-2001||08:47 PM||||Okay here's the scoop. This is a d@mn nice 85 GT. 130,000 miles showing. Recall work has been done. The vinyl on top of the radio pod is peeling up just a bit. The finish on the <I>tops</I> of the dash corners has been been rubbed through. Little bit of yellow plastic showing through. Other than that, the interior is flawless. Seats almost look new. Even has the floormats. Has a Panasonic radio. Starts right up. Sounds good. Has a small hole in the muffler, but manifolds are good. Clutch feels good. No trouble shifting into 1st or reverse. (It's a 4-speed). AC seems to blow really cold. The outside is about 8.5 of 10. It's been repainted (at least in places), but the paint looks good. Some <I>very</I> minor cracks in the front fascia. Rear fascia is flawless. The only thing that bothers me is that the LF fender doesn't seem to fit just right. The gap between the fender and door is a bit wider at the top than at the bottom. The second coat of paint (or clearcoat?) is starting to peel at the top corner of the fender. Missing the 6" piece of trim behind the wheel. The lock on the drivers door is messed up, and the power lock on that side doesn't seem to work correctly, either. <BR>The wing is missing some of the screws that hold it to the supports. Feels like it's hinged at the rear.<BR>Unfortunately, I didn't have time to drive it, and I neglected to check all the rest of the power accessories, and lights. (It's loaded. Even has power mirrors and rear defrost.) The guy said that $2150 was bottom dollar. (He's got "$2950" on the windshield. Along with "5 speed".)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Told him I'd pass it along to the Forum.<BR> <P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 03-30-2001).]||||reg||1
